Q: authenticating mock user when testing in quarkus A: <p>A more convinient way to mock the security is to use Quarkus' security testing features:</p>
<p><a href="https://quarkus.io/guides/security-testing#testing-security" rel="noreferrer">https://quarkus.io/guides/security-testing#testing-security</a></p>
<p>Including</p>
<pre><code>&lt;dependency&gt;
    &lt;groupId&gt;io.quarkus&lt;/groupId&gt;
    &lt;artifactId&gt;quarkus-test-security&lt;/artifactId&gt;
    &lt;scope&gt;test&lt;/scope&gt;
&lt;/dependency&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>allows you to write</p>
<pre><code>@Test
@TestSecurity(authorizationEnabled = false)
void someTestMethod() {
...
}

@Test
@TestSecurity(user = &quot;testUser&quot;, roles = {&quot;admin&quot;, &quot;user&quot;})
void otherTestMethod() {
...
}
</code></pre>

